WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.181
Gardening is my graffiti.

00:00:02.181 --> 00:00:03.500
I grow my art.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.640
I&nbsp;beautify lawns, parkways.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.038
I use the garden, the soil,

00:00:07.038 --> 00:00:08.831
like it's a piece of cloth,

00:00:08.831 --> 00:00:11.841
and the&nbsp;plants and the trees,

00:00:11.841 --> 00:00:13.747
that's my embellishment for that cloth.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.432
I live in a food desert.

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:17.734
So me&nbsp;and my group, 
L.A. Green Grounds,

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.359
we got together and we 
started planting my food forest,

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:22.060
fruit&nbsp;trees, you know, the whole nine.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.398
I have witnessed my garden

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:26.625
become a tool for the education,

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:29.280
a&nbsp;tool for the transformation
 of my neighborhood.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.043
To change the community,

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:34.496
you have to change&nbsp;the 
composition of the soil.

00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:36.176
We are the soil.

00:00:36.176 --> 00:00:39.910
I want us all to become 
ecolutionary renegades,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.801
gangstas, gangsta gardeners.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.928
What I'm talking about is 
putting people to work,

00:00:43.928 --> 00:00:46.135
and getting kids off the street,

00:00:46.135 --> 00:00:47.864
and letting them know the joy,

00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:48.973
the pride

00:00:48.973 --> 00:00:52.434
and the honor in growing your&nbsp;own food.

